    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** stands out as our premier option with a 73.47 efficiency score. Facing Dobnak, **Butler** benefits from a high-upside matchup against a soft-tossing starter with a 4.70 xERA, amplified by an ideal cleanup spot in the order. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains an elite foundational piece despite a modest platoon downgrade, posting a 69.84 score by virtue of his consistent ability to drive production regardless of the arm on the mound. While **Daulton Varsho** carries a high 67.97 score due to his power-speed profile, managers should monitor the official lineup card, as his status remains pending. **Jonathan Aranda** also provides significant value (69.45) as he slots into the #3 hole against Bieber; his dynamic platoon edge against a right-hander is the primary driver in elevating him above his base projection today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the periphery involved **Yainer Diaz**, who landed at a 52.98 efficiency score. While he possesses the talent to exceed expectations, the uncertainty of an assumed #9 spot in the batting order, combined with the difficulty of facing Grayson Rodriguez, kept him in the lower tier of our active roster. **Braden Montgomery** narrowly earned the final UTIL spot with a 53.25 score; his versatility and favorable matchup against Holmes provide a higher floor than our depth options like **Tyler Freeman**, **Matt Chapman**, or **Gleyber Torres**. We are currently managing significant roster noise due to the inactivity of **Cal Raleigh**, **Bryce Harper**, and **Will Smith**, the latter of whom remains sidelined on the IL. As we continue to navigate the season, keep a close eye on **Justin Crawford**, **Masyn Winn**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Alex Freeland**, who are currently waiting in the wings should we need to adjust our approach to secure those high-value stolen bases.\n\nRisk remains centered on the weather and the pending statuses for **Yainer Diaz**, **Dylan Beavers**, and **Daulton Varsho**. Should those lineups shift negatively, we risk efficiency drops in the #9 and #6 spots, respectively. Furthermore, while **Jung Hoo Lee** faces a tough test against Williams, his ability to manipulate the zone helps mitigate the threat of a sub-3.00 xERA arm, though he is the most susceptible to a total collapse if the matchup remains unfavorable.",
